      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Phenoperidine is mainly metabolised in the liver, and has a biliary and urinary elimination. Because its analgesic effects are fast and prolonged, this drug is often used in pediatric intensive care units, due to its interesting pharmacologic properties (mild cardiac and respiratory depression)."},
